The verification layer remains fail-open. Most damaging: `run_ac()` records failed checks but publishes anyway.

## Critical

1. `run_ac()` publishes despite failed or absent reconciliation.

   [electors/run.py:387](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:387)

   `found["residuals"]`, `measured < run.parts`, and `matching < measured` are copied into `run` but never set `run.error`. Execution proceeds to `write_shard()`.

   Wrongly passing input: every extracted part has fewer rows than its printed total, or every `side.json` has `summary=None`. The shard is written, `run.error` remains empty, and the CLI exits successfully. This permits arbitrary row loss.

2. Missing published evidence disables the constituency completeness check entirely.

   [electors/run.py:297](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:297), [electors/run.py:378](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:378)

   `published_totals()` returns `{}` when the dataset is absent, contains no matching AC, or every matching row has `electors_total=None`. Then `if published` is false and no expected-part check runs.

   Wrongly passing input: missing `dataset/parts.jsonl.gz` plus an empty or partial work directory. `read()` can return `[]`, the empty `inside` set skips the AC identity check, and `run_ac()` writes a successful empty shard.

3. Losing some composites inside a part is still silently accepted.

   [electors/stage1.py:273](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/stage1.py:273), [electors/stage2.py:237](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/stage2.py:237), [electors/stage2.py:124](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/stage2.py:124)

   Both `done()` and `ready()` require only `any(composite*.png)`. `read_part()` iterates files that exist rather than filenames declared in `placements.json`; missing declared composites are never noticed.

   Wrongly passing input: placements declare `composite000.png` and `composite001.png`, but only `composite000.png` remains. Both readiness checks return true; tiles assigned to `composite001.png` produce no words and therefore no rows. If that image held supplements, reconciliation can still match the main total exactly.

4. A row-cache filename alone proves that a part was successfully read.

   [electors/run.py:151](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:151)

   If `rows.jsonl` exists, `read()` bypasses `stage2.ready()`, source identity, stage versions, manifest/placement consistency, and expected row count.

   Wrongly passing input: an empty `rows.jsonl`, a stale cache from an older parser, or a cache belonging to different stage-one artifacts. It is accepted as complete and can permanently cache zero or partial rows.

5. `published_totals()` keys verification by an OCR-derived part number that is already wrong in the committed evidence.

   [electors/run.py:303](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:303)

   It uses `row["part_no"]`, silently overwriting duplicate keys, instead of establishing identity from the source filename/`part_no_file`.

   This is active, not hypothetical: [dataset/parts.jsonl.gz](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/dataset/parts.jsonl.gz) contains 185 `part_no != part_no_file` rows across 101 of 126 ACs. There are four dictionary collisions. For example, AC1 has no published key 111 and instead has key 1114; AC22 reports 305 unique parts from 307 source records, losing keys 53 and 54. Those real parts are consequently invisible to `struck_off_check()`.

6. The struck-off check self-cancels exactly the failure it is intended to detect.

   [electors/run.py:265](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:265)

   `implied` is computed from extracted row counts, not independently established gross totals:

   `implied = extracted main + extracted extra - published net`.

   Wrongly passing input: the roll prints 873 entries, net 850, with 23 deletions; extraction drops all 23 deleted rows and keeps 850 live rows. The function returns `detected=0`, `implied=0`, `diff=0`. `render_report()` prints no struck-off warning because both aggregate values are zero.

## High

7. Stage-one failures do not fail `run_ac()`.

   [electors/run.py:339](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:339)

   Failed preparations are placed in `run.failed_parts`, but success is determined only by `run.error`.

   Wrongly passing input: one of 100 parts fails and only 99 are ready. The separate 99% guard also passes 99/100, so the shard is published and the command exits zero while recording a failed part.

8. The completeness guard deliberately accepts missing parts.

   [electors/run.py:380](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/run.py:380)

   The precise condition is `run.parts < len(published) * 0.99`, not equality.

   Wrongly passing input: 208 of 210 parts, 99 of 100, or 302 of AC22’s 307 actual source parts given its already-collapsed 305-key published map. All report success.

9. Missing or failed closing-page verification becomes an ordinary successful part read.

   [electors/stage2.py:170](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/stage2.py:170), [electors/stage2.py:105](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/stage2.py:105)

   `summary_from_vision()` returns `None` for a missing `summary_page.png`, no Vision response, empty cached words, or an unparseable response. `read_part()` does not set `result.error`.

   Wrongly passing input: stage one records `summary=None` but loses `summary_page.png`. Rows are read and cached, the part is merely “unmeasured,” and finding 1 lets the constituency publish successfully.

10. The repack verifier reports success after comparing zero tiles.

   [electors/verify.py:41](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/verify.py:41), [electors/verify.py:77](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/verify.py:77), [electors/verify.py:134](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/verify.py:134), [electors/verify.py:209](/Users/soodoku/Documents/GitHub/assam_elex_rolls_2026/electors/verify.py:209)

   An empty manifest and `{}` placements produce `tiles == placements == 0`, no problems, an empty pixel sample, and `PartCheck.ok == True`. The report then says “every check passed.”

